sentences.text:
It is mainly contended by the learned Advocate for the appellant that the learned tribunal has erred in considering 50% of liability and negligence on the part of the driver of the truck which was insured with the appellant and in fact no negligence could have been said to have been committed on the part of the driver of the truck;
that the road where the accident took place is the National Highway and the truck was lying on the left side of the road and ambulance dashed with the truck from its behind;
that as per the say of the claimant they were taking the deceased to the hospital at Ahmedabad as he was sick and as they were in a hurry, the vehicle was going in full speed and the learned tribunal has failed to appreciate that the National Highway must be very wide road with heavy vehicular traffic and normally no one would keep the vehicle in the middle of the road; the learned tribunal has also not considered the fact that the ambulance must be having its own light and the light could be reflected upto 20 meters ahead and if the driver of the ambulance was driving the vehicle in controllable speed, the accident could have been avoided; that the driver of the ambulance ought to have taken more care which is expected of a prudent driver when he was transporting a sick person and the learned tribunal has grossly erred in attributing 50% negligence to the driver of the truck and hence the appeal must be allowed.
10.

